Rodney can be tricky at times, even for a level 30, maxed-stat, AC -45 
kick-ass wizard who can cast *all* the spells at 0% failure (but with 
naught but Magicbane for a physical weapon).

I had decided that polypiling the whole heap of equipment from an 
especially large military barracks might turn into something useful, so 
I was hauling tons of heavy armor when suddenly Rodney dropped by. I was 
only two spaces from the nearest pile, and I figured that Rodney 
wouldn't manage to do much in the time it would take to dump the load, 
so I decided to ignore him.

Whereupon Rodney proceeded to steal the Amulet of Yendor, the Eye of the 
Aethiopica, and (somehow he managed to produce) a wand of digging. Now 
he was magic protected, my most powerful weapons FoD and magic missile 
couldn't hurt him, and I was left with only my +3 Magicbane. Things 
started turning nasty as he summoned hordes of nasties, my power dropped 
(due to lack of the Eye), and Rodney kept escaping by zapping his wand 
of digging.

Eventually I prevailed, none the worse for wear, but once again Nethack 
managed to put some real fright into a seasoned hacker.

